From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, kernelbase, cmd: Junctions read back as junctions (6039)

A junction (IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT) was stored like a symbolic link
and read back as one. Its Unix link target now ends in a slash, and
FileAttributeTagInformation, FSCTL_GET_REPARSE_POINT (the mount point
layout) and directory entries report IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT for it.
Directory entries carry a reparse point's tag in the EA size, as NTFS
does, and FindFirstFile (A and W) reports it in dwReserved0. cmd's
mklink /J makes junctions; it said they were not supported.
---
